  <info>
    <title><command>zypper</command> commands not modifying the file system</title><!-- can be changed via merge in the assembly -->
    <!--add author's email address-->
    <meta name="maintainer" content="jsindelarova@suse.com" its:translate="no"/>
    <abstract><!-- can be changed via merge in the assembly -->
      <para>
       Operations that query external repositories or the local database do not require write access to the root file system. Because these commands do not alter the system state, they bypass the transactional wrapper and do not create a Btrfs snapshot.
      </para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <para>
  The following <command>zypper</command> commands function exactly as they do on a standard system:
  </para>
  <itemizedlist>
  <listitem>
  <para><command>zypper search <replaceable>PACKAGE_NAME</replaceable></command></para>
  </listitem>
  <listitem>
  <para><command>zypper info <replaceable>PACKAGE_NAME</replaceable></command></para>
  </listitem>
  <listitem>
  <para>Repository modification commands</para>
  </listitem>
  </itemizedlist>
  <para>For more details about the above mentioned commands, refer to the zypper article.</para> 
</topic>
